CMS EnvelopedData, key agreement: mqvSinglePass-sha256kdf-scheme (1.3.132.1.15.1), id-aes128-wrap, id-aes128-CBC

NOT a conformance vector. Generated with bc-java 1.86, whose 1-Pass ECMQV gave the X9.63 KDF the raw
addedukm - or nothing, when there was none - as its SharedInfo, instead of the DER-encoded ECC-CMS-SharedInfo
that RFC 5753 sec. 3.2.2 and 7.2 require. That is the form bc-java produced from 1.53 to 1.86, and a
conformant receiver rejects it. Kept so that a receiver's backward-compatibility retry for such messages
(bc-java: the org.bouncycastle.cms.allow_legacy_keyagree_kdf property; bc-csharp: CmsAllowLegacyKeyAgreeKdf)
can be tested; the conformant equivalents are in ../mqv-ukm.

